Z||000014||FieroJoe||05-28-2001||12:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>Just make sure you get the right John Deere green paint.. and spell your girlfriend's name right on the water tank! They hate when you spell it wrong...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Funny thing is, our old water tower in my town was tagged every year by the senior class.  It looked pretty crappy too, because all they would do is put a line through the previous year numbers and paint on the new one.  Im surprised nobody fell and died, it was way up there.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000015||frontal lobe||05-28-2001||01:35 AM||||I'm all for you tagging-as long as it is on your own possessions or property.<P>If you are talking about doing it on anyone else's property without express consent, including "public" property-which belongs to everyone-then no matter how "beautiful" it is, it's still vandalism.||||reg||1
